{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 119, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a skip connection on edge 0 with a 3x3 conv gives large gains (e.g. +43, +7 on C10), while replacing none or conv1x1 gives about zero."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a skip on edge 4 to a 3x3 conv helps much more (+35 in the all-skip parent) than adding a conv where edge 4 is none or conv1x1 (about +0.5)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing an avg_pool on edge 2 with a conv gives a large gain (+27 on C10 in observation 73), while edge 2 edits on other ops are near zero."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a weak avg_pool on the final edge for a 3x3 conv yields +6 to +15, more than from conv1x1 (+3 to +8) or from none/skip."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 3 hurts most when edge 5 is already none, since the cell then loses its main path to the output (-78 and -21 on IN16)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the direct edge 3 is absent, edge 2 (often a skip) becomes harmful, so removing it gives a gain (+11 on IN16) instead of the small loss seen with edge 3 present."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Downgrading a 3x3 conv on edge 0 to a skip loses accuracy (-11 to -17 in one parent), while replacing none or avg_pool with skip tends to help."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": 